# What the image build does NOT need.
#
# **Deliberately short.** More than the obvious is excluded at your peril: the build embeds files
# from outside `crates/` at compile time and a missing one fails as a confusing macro error rather
# than as a missing file. `crates/cli/src/selftest.rs` `include_str!`s the conformance telemetry
# out of the CONTRACT SUBMODULE and the derived corpus out of `conformance/`; `storage` embeds
# `CLICKHOUSE_VERSION` and its migration SQL. So `contract/` and `conformance/` stay.
#
# **The submodule must be checked out before building**, or those embeds have nothing to read:
#   git submodule update --init --depth 1 contract/inference-events

# Build output. The largest thing here by far, and never an input.
target/
.cargo-home/
.rustup-home/

# Git metadata. The contract submodule's FILES live in the working tree and survive this; only
# the repository's own history is excluded.
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Local tooling: `.tools/clickhouse` is a host-architecture binary fetched for local tests. The
# image fetches and hash-verifies its OWN engine in the first stage, and letting a developer's
# arm64 Mach-O near an amd64 image is exactly the confusion that stage exists to prevent.
.tools/
*.tgz

# CI and prose. None of it is an input to the binary.
.github/
docs/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.claude/
